{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to His heart</b> — He did not reveal the matter to the prophet at that time; only on the day that He commanded Moses to write the Torah did He reveal to him that when Noah offered his sacrifice, it ascended before Him for acceptance, and He decreed not to again strike every living thing. And I have already written concerning this (Ramban on Genesis 6:6) a mystic hint alluded to by our Rabbis, of blessed memory. And the sense of \"for the sake of man\" is that for his sake they were punished, and if man had not sinned, they would have been spared even though they too had corrupted their way." "<b>For the imagination of the heart of man is evil from his youth</b> — This teaches merit on their behalf: that their formation is evil in the days of youth and not in the days of old age, and if so, there is no reason to strike every living thing because of these two reasons. And the sense of the mem in מנעוריו is that from the beginning of youth it is upon them, as they said (Genesis Rabbah 34:10), from the time he is weaned to come forth from his mother's womb, the evil impulse is placed within him. Or it may say: for from his youth — that is, because of it — the evil of the impulse in man will be, for it causes him to sin. And some say it is like בנעוריו (in his youth), and similar to it, \"from before one stone was placed upon another in the temple of YHWH\" (Haggai 2:15), and likewise, \"this is the land that you shall allot as inheritance to the tribes of Israel\" (Ezekiel 48:29)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The closing examples from Haggai 2:15 and Ezekiel 48:29 illustrate the comparative use of the prefixed mem (מן) meaning 'from/before' in temporal and spatial constructions; the second example with תפילו (Qere for תפיל) follows the ketiv form as Ramban quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:21.776215350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}